  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Usage",
      "text": "`TagsInput` provides a way to enter multiple values. It can be used with suggestions or without them.\n`TagsInput` is similar to [MultiSelect](/core/multi-select), but it allows entering custom values.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Controlled",
      "text": "`TagsInput` value must be an array of strings, other types are not supported.\n`onChange` function is called with an array of strings as a single argument.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Controlled search value",
      "text": "You can control search value with `searchValue` and `onSearchChange` props:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Clearable",
      "text": "Set `clearable` prop to display the clear button in the right section. The button is not displayed\nwhen:\n\n- The component does not have a value\n- The component is disabled\n- The component is read only",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Max selected values",
      "text": "You can limit the number of selected values with `maxTags` prop. This will not allow adding more values\nonce the limit is reached.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accept value on blur",
      "text": "By default, if the user types a value and blurs the input, the value is added to the list.\nYou can change this behavior by setting `acceptValueOnBlur` to `false`. In this case, the value is added\nonly when the user presses `Enter` or clicks on a suggestion.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Allow duplicates",
      "text": "By default `TagsInput` does not allow to add duplicate values, but you can change this behavior by\nsetting `allowDuplicates` prop. Value is considered duplicate if it is already present in the `value` array,\nregardless of the case and trailing whitespace.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Split chars",
      "text": "By default, `TagsInput` splits values by comma (`,`), you can change this behavior by setting\n`splitChars` prop to an array of strings. All values from `splitChars` cannot be included in the final value.\nValues are also splitted on paste.\n\nExample of splitting by `,`, `|` and space:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "With suggestions",
      "text": "`TagsInput` can be used with suggestions, it will render suggestions list under input and allow to select\nsuggestions with keyboard or mouse. Note that user is not limited to suggestions, it is still possible to\nenter custom values. If you want to allow values only from suggestions, use [MultiSelect](/core/multi-select) component instead.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sort options",
      "text": "By default, options are sorted by their position in the data array. You can change this behavior\nwith `filter` function:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "renderOption",
      "text": "`renderOption` callback allows you to customize option rendering. It is called with option object.\nThe function must return a React node.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Scrollable dropdown",
      "text": "By default, the options list is wrapped with [ScrollArea.Autosize](/core/scroll-area).\nYou can control dropdown max-height with `maxDropdownHeight` prop if you do not change the default settings.\n\nIf you want to use native scrollbars, set `withScrollArea={false}`. Note that in this case,\nyou will need to change dropdown styles with [Styles API](/styles/styles-api).",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Disabled options",
      "text": "When option is disabled, it cannot be selected and is ignored in keyboard navigation.\nNote that user can still enter disabled option as a value. If you want to prohibit certain values,\nuse controlled component and filter them out in `onChange` function.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inside Popover",
      "text": "To use `TagsInput` inside popover, you need to set `withinPortal: false`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Control dropdown opened state",
      "text": "You can control dropdown opened state with `dropdownOpened` prop. Additionally,\nyou can use `onDropdownClose` and `onDropdownOpen` to listen to dropdown opened state changes.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dropdown position",
      "text": "By default, the dropdown is displayed below the input if there is enough space; otherwise it is displayed above the input.\nYou can change this behavior by setting `position` and `middlewares` props, which are passed down to the\nunderlying [Popover](/core/popover) component.\n\nExample of dropdown that is always displayed above the input:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dropdown animation",
      "text": "By default, dropdown animations are disabled. To enable them, you can set `transitionProps`,\nwhich will be passed down to the underlying [Transition](/core/transition) component.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dropdown width",
      "text": "To change dropdown width, set `width` prop in `comboboxProps`. By default,\ndropdown width is equal to the input width.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Read only",
      "text": "Set `readOnly` to make the input read only. When `readOnly` is set,\n`TagsInput` will not show suggestions and will not call `onChange` function.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Disabled",
      "text": "Set `disabled` to disable the input. When `disabled` is set,\nuser cannot interact with the input and `TagsInput` will not show suggestions.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Error state",
      "text": "To set `aria-label` on the clear button, use `clearButtonProps`. Note that it is required\nonly when `clearable` is set.",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
